From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:05:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] port 2ac15656 389ef5c8 67ec083d: verify: the last stage
 draws a batch window's sampled rows right behind its graph (opt-in
 STRATA_EARLY_SAMPLE=1)

batch_launch enqueues sample_rows' draws on the stage stream right behind the window (and its commit graph), so
batch_poll finds them done and launches nothing.  A row whose draw batch_poll would make differently (its slot's
sampling set meanwhile, same_sampling over every SamplerParams field, floats bit for bit) is drawn again there,
over the same logits.  init_slots reserves the split sampler's scratch (sample_tokens_reserve), so no cudaMalloc
runs while the window is in flight.  sampler_same_test (CPU) binds SamplerParams' 14 fields by name (389ef5c8);
the Metal stub for sample_tokens_reserve (67ec083d).  Not measured on its own yet (TESTLOG #77: greedy A/B only).

(cherry picked from commits 2ac15656ea59, 389ef5c85edd and 67ec083dd01a)

Port to v0.2.12 (sample_rows now goes through slot_row_draw, 541a2fac: slot penalties and logit bias in batch
windows):
- our row_draw() is gone; early_row_draw() is slot_row_draw's draw for the rows that stage nothing: a sampled
  slot (not greedy, temperature > 0) with no active penalty and no logit bias.  Penalty rows need slot_tail_ and a
  cudaMalloc'd / cudaMemcpyAsync'd history (slot_hist_d_), bias rows read a per-slot device buffer that
  set_slot_logit_bias may rewrite: both are drawn in batch_poll as upstream does, and so are greedy rows with a
  bias or penalties (slot_row_draw returns 1 for them).
- sample_rows skips a row only when it was drawn early, slot_row_draw staged no history for it, and
  same_sampling(sp, the early draw) holds.
- b_early_sp_ is sized kWindowMaxT (16-row windows); the mask stays 32 bits.
- sample_tokens_reserve: v0.2.12's sample_tokens still sizes the split scratch as 16 rows x blocks x kSelMax.
- only batch_launch draws early; batch_launch_rows (deferred commit) and run_slot_rows keep their path
  (stage_batch clears the mask).  With STRATA_EARLY_SAMPLE unset nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
